{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 29, :comments ["<b>And she shall bring them to the priest.</b> From where do we know that she immerses by day? Scripture says: ״והביאה אותם אל הכהן אל פתח אהל מועד״ — but if the sun's setting were intermixed (i.e., if she were bringing them at the approach of sundown), it teaches that she immerses by day."], :book :leviticus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {0 "The phrase מעורבת שמש, literally 'mixed with sun,' refers to the period near sunset; the halakhic inference is that since her offerings must reach the priest while it is still recognizably day, her immersion must likewise be performed by day."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:12:36.041190809Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}